test-data/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The local object store, behind r2:// URIs. NONE of it is committed.
#
# There was a plan to commit the light half of it -- crops, journals, parquets,
# ~9 MB per folder -- so a `git pull` would reproduce the whole review panel on
# the other person's machine with no server and no cloud account. That plan
# assumed a PRIVATE repo. This repo is public, so it is off.
#
# Face crops and embeddings are biometric data under India's DPDP Act. On a
# public repo that means real people's faces, permanently, indexed. Not worth
# saving one person a 10-minute setup.
#
# If this ever moves to a private repo and sharing the panel matters again, the
# rule to restore is: exclude prev/, thumb/, *.f32 and generated *.html (98% of
# the bytes, and the panel asks for none of them -- measured), commit the rest.
.wff-store/

# The Google API key, if this checkout keeps its own. The one on this machine
# lives in ~/.wff/settings.env, outside the repo entirely.
.env

.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
